<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10644" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-strĕpo</span></b> ,
		ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. n., to resound, sound loudly</i> or <i>boisterously, to make a noise</i> (post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus tota constrepebat hymenaeum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 154, 23</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 11</span></i>, p. 261,
			34.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of a vivid speech: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">horum omnium et testimoniis et exemplis
					constrepebat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					4, 1, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
